1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Jose Abecassis - in his book Genealogia Hebraica - Porgugal e Gibraltar  'He was one of the first six Jews who in 1819 disembarqued on S. Miguel, Azores.  On December 29, 1824 he made a contract, in Li
2 CONC sbon with Mimon Abohbot so that he would go to Angra Do Heroismo, Terceira, Azores, for a period of one year as his cashier to sell farms, with the obligation to move to the other islands, and with a monthly orders of $6000 reis. 
2 CONC Since by the end of the year he had not recieved any orders, Mimon Abohbot, accused him before the local authorities. Then Salao Buzaglo was under the obligation, by judicial order from September 12, 1827 to pay $96,000 reis withi
2 CONC n 24 hours. The handwriting, spelling and calligraphy by Salao Buzaglo  which was written in Portuguese was less than rudimentary.  In 1825 he exported (esteiras) from Terceira to Lisbon, and in 1826, from Gibraltar on bord the Ya
2 CONC cht "Senhora da Pax" he received Terceira tea, coffee and English farms in the the amounts of 1150$270 réis. Established on Rua da Sé, in Angra, he sold by bulk and at a discount, it was in 19828 that he was cohersed by the author
2 CONC ities at the request of his landlord, Jeronimo Jose Toesteto vacate his shop : The Angresian merchants who represented by Manuel Menes Correia, were hostile to the Jews of their trade, and made war on them. They did better with Sa
2 CONC lao Buzaglo, because he was a foreigner and he did not have the same commercial privileges the Portuguese had and he couldn´t get the same offers. Salao Buzaglo lived with his family at the house on Rua Nova da Matriz, in Ponta De
2 CONC lgada, S. Miguel. Azores, builty by him and where he worked and that laer belonged to Mrio Pacheco Leal. In 1836 he was one of the founders of the Synagogue, Sahar Hassamaims of Ponta Delgada. His contribution to the Synagogue in 
2 CONC the year 1868-69 was 16,550 réis. At that time he was the Director (Parnass). There is a beautiful picture of him in oil, with a plate that has his name and the datesÑ Born 1790, Died 1868, painted by Giorgio Marini in S. Miguel, 
2 CONC who signed it and gave it to him in 1869, it belongs to the author José Maria Abecassis, third grandson of his sister in law, Julia Conquy. He was married two times, Married the first time in Ponta Delgada, on Wednesday, 2 of Siva
2 CONC n, 5579 ( 1819) to Simhah Tedeschi Conquy, Born - 1793. Died June 19 1863 in S. Miguel. May she rest in peace.  She was the daughter of Isaac Conquy and Sarah Tedeschi. Samuel Sebag and Shalom Ben Jacob Abecassis were the oficiant
2 CONC s and witnesses. The Quetuba is in the collection of Jose Abecassis since 1958. This was the oldest wedding that we are aware of among the Jews in Portugal since their return. The following year Judah Bensabat Zagury and Luna Amza
2 CONC lak married.
