3 CTRY Gibraltar
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 JAN 1839
2 PLAC Gibraltar
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 TITL Don
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moroccan and Austrian consul at Gibraltar; president of the Jewish community there, and of the chamber of commerce; died in 1839. When Sardinia sent a fleet against Morocco, Benoliel was enabled, in his consular ca
2 CONC pacity, to settle the differences amicably. He earned special credit by his services to the Jewish community of Tangier. On account of a quarrel that had taken place between two Jews in a synagogue of that city, the governor, with
2 CONC  the sultan's consent, had all the synagogues of the city demolished. When the sultan Muley Abd al-Raḥman visited Tangier two years later, Benoliel, who was much respected by him, declining all honors for himself, secured permissi
2 CONC on for the reerection of the synagogues. In memory of this noble self-denial, a special memorial prayer is offered on every Day ofAtonement in the synagogues of Tangier. Judah Benoliel also possessed the full confidence of Cardina
2 CONC l Mastai-Ferretti, afterward Pope Pius IX. When the latter returned to Italy from Chile he entrusted Benoliel with large sums of money.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography: Report of the Anglo-Jewish Association, 1877-78, p. 113. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/3007-benoliel-don-judah
2 CONT
2 CONT More about Don Judah Benoliel here: http://gibraltar-intro.blogspot.co.uk/2013/08/1772-benoliel-family-yahuda-bulil.html
