2 CONT Pontus Fürstenberg (4 October 1827 – 10 April 1902) was a Swedish art collector and merchant from a Jewish family. He was married to Göthilda Magnus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pontus Fürstenberg was born at Östra Hamngatan 26, in Gothenburg, Sweden. His family had arrived in Sweden at the beginning of the 19th century. Pontus was the oldest child, and his parents were wholesalers [https://www.geni.com/p
2 CONC eople/Levy-F%C3%BCrstenberg/6000000013823545752 Levy Fürstenberg] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Rosa-Warburg/6000000013823564197 Rosa Warburg]. Levy also owned the textile company Levy Fürstenberg & Co, which provided the famil
2 CONC y a good economic base.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pontus did poorly in school. His grades were mediocre, but he did well enough to be able to attend the Handelsintitutet (Institute of Trade). At the age of 26, he became part-owner in his [https://www.geni.com/people/Levy-F%C3%BCr
2 CONC stenberg/6000000013823545752 father's] textile company. A short way from the company lived the wealthy [https://www.geni.com/people/Eduard-Magnus/6000000008349721450 Magnus family]. Both families spent a lot of time together, and 
2 CONC it was here that Pontus met their only daughter, [https://www.geni.com/people/G%C3%B6thilda-Charlotta-Magnus/4366089571110034039 Göthilda Magnus], who would later become his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT During this time, Pontus started to engage himself in local politics, and at the age of 42 was appointed leader of the city council (stadsfullmäktige) in 1869. He was also involved with many community activities, including serving
2 CONC  as Vice President of the Gothenburg Ancient Monument Society.
